WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.292 --> 00:00:01.667
[woman] Wait, you want me
to tell 'em what happened?

2
00:00:02.417 --> 00:00:05.208
Well, two people got crabs,
and they were spreading.

3
00:00:05.292 --> 00:00:06.917
We were all very hyper about it.

4
00:00:07.042 --> 00:00:09.000
I have to go shower some people.

5
00:00:09.083 --> 00:00:10.333
[chuckles] I'll see you later.

6
00:00:12.375 --> 00:00:16.375
[man 1] I wanted to be part of the world,
but I didn't see anyone like me in it.

7
00:00:16.458 --> 00:00:19.417
I hear about a summer camp
for the handicapped, run by hippies.

8
00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:21.917
Somebody said you probably
will smoke dope with the counselors.

9
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:24.542
[chuckles] And I'm like, "Sign me up!"

10
00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:29.083
Come to Camp Jened and find yourself.

11
00:00:29.167 --> 00:00:31.208
There I was! I was at Woodstock.

12
00:00:33.042 --> 00:00:36.042
[man 2] You wouldn't be picked
to be on the team back home.

13
00:00:36.125 --> 00:00:38.292
But at Jened,
you had to go up to bat.

14
00:00:39.667 --> 00:00:43.083
Even when we were that young,
we helped empower each other.

15
00:00:43.167 --> 00:00:45.375
It was allowing us to recognize

16
00:00:45.458 --> 00:00:48.792
that the status quo
is not what it needed to be.

17
00:00:50.125 --> 00:00:52.250
[woman 2]
The world always wants us dead.

18
00:00:52.333 --> 00:00:53.667
We live with that reality.

19
00:00:54.167 --> 00:00:56.583
[man 1] At the time,
so many kids just like me

20
00:00:56.667 --> 00:00:58.417
were being sent to institutions.

21
00:00:59.417 --> 00:01:01.583
It was just a continual struggle.

22
00:01:01.667 --> 00:01:06.625
Most disabled people, like myself,
are unable to use public transportation.

23
00:01:06.708 --> 00:01:09.500
[man 1] We needed
a civil rights law of our own.

24
00:01:12.583 --> 00:01:15.708
[reporter] A rehabilitation program
has been vetoed by the president

25
00:01:15.792 --> 00:01:17.375
because it was cost prohibitive.

26
00:01:17.458 --> 00:01:19.083
[woman 3] We decided we were
gonna have a demonstration.

27
00:01:19.167 --> 00:01:20.333
[woman 4] You get the call to action.

28
00:01:20.417 --> 00:01:21.500
"To the barricades!"

29
00:01:22.417 --> 00:01:24.042
[reporter] A small army of the handicapped

30
00:01:24.125 --> 00:01:26.542
have occupied this building
for the past 11 days.

31
00:01:26.625 --> 00:01:29.875
[man 1] So many people from Camp Jened
found their way into the building.

32
00:01:31.375 --> 00:01:33.083
[woman 2] The FBI cut off the phones.

33
00:01:33.167 --> 00:01:35.042
The deaf people went,
"We know what to do."

34
00:01:35.125 --> 00:01:38.000
That's how we communicated
to the people outside the building.

35
00:01:38.083 --> 00:01:40.083
The Black Panther Party
would bring a hot meal.

36
00:01:40.167 --> 00:01:41.000
We were like this.

37
00:01:41.083 --> 00:01:44.500
[man over PA] We are the strongest
political force in this country.

38
00:01:44.667 --> 00:01:48.667
We will no longer allow the government
to oppress disabled individuals.

39
00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:52.083
And I would appreciate it if you would
stop shaking your head in agreement

40
00:01:52.167 --> 00:01:55.125
when I don't think you understand
what we are talking about.

41
00:01:58.375 --> 00:02:01.833
[man 1] What we saw at that camp
was that our lives could be better.

42
00:02:01.917 --> 00:02:03.042
-[boy] Go!
-[man 3] Go!

43
00:02:06.542 --> 00:02:09.458
[woman 5] If you don't demand
what you believe in for yourself,

44
00:02:10.833 --> 00:02:12.208
you're not gonna get it.

45
00:02:12.292 --> 00:02:15.125
♪ I sailed for pleasure ♪

46
00:02:15.208 --> 00:02:17.500
♪ I sailed for pleasure ♪

47
00:02:17.583 --> 00:02:20.792
Would you like to see the
handicapped people depicted as people?

48
00:02:22.208 --> 00:02:22.958
Excuse me?